tags: event

= Liberal Demands

  The Liberals are surprised to see the Labour government survive a year in office. They believed it would have crashed by now, whether to infighting or through a vote of no confidence. However, seeing now that Labour can hold it together. They feel some demands are in order. After all, why support a socialist party for nothing. In exchange for further toleration, the liberals ask that Labour fulfill a certain amount of their demands every year. Or else face a vote of no confidence. 

- @cap: Let's hope they're not unreasonable...


@cap

The Liberals presents us with a list of demands, and a few of their red lines.

[? if capital_levy = 0 : - No capital Levy!!!! ?]

[? if tax_goal = 1 : - Cut taxes ?]

[? if agricultural_goal = 1 : - Persue some agricultural nationalisation ?]

[? if communists_goal = 1 : - Persecute Communists ?]

[? if labor_goal = 1 : - Seek compromise in labor disputes. ?]

[? if electoral_goal = 1 : - Pass bill for Preportional Representation ?]

#[? if womens_goal = 1 : - Equalise voting rights for men and women ?]

[? if reichswehr_goal = 1 : - Reduce funding for the Military. ?]

They say 4 of these are to be fulfilled in a year. Otherwise, they will call a vote of no confidence on our government
